code></strong>. This is done separately from the return statement.</p>
<p>The maximum path sum of the entire tree is found by keeping track of the=
 largest path sum formed at every node.</p>
<p><strong>Handling negative path sums</strong><br>
One final thing to note is that we shouldn=E2=80=99t include the values of =
<code>left_sum</code> or <code>right_sum</code> if either is negative, as t=
hey wouldn=E2=80=99t contribute to a maximum sum. We can do this by setting=
 their values to 0 if they=E2=80=99re negative, which is the same as exclud=
ing the left or right path from the sum.</p>
